{"name":"Oro","hex":"#c29436","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Oro","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Oro"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hora (dance)","blocks":[{"text":"Hora, also known as horo and oro, is a type of circle dance traditionally performed in Southeast Europe. Circle dances with similar names are found in Bulgaria, Romania, Moldova, North Macedonia, Greece and Turkey, and among ethnic minorities such as the Ashkenazi Jews, Sephardic Jews and the Roma."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Tanec_folk_ensemble_Macedonia_1.jpg/330px-Tanec_folk_ensemble_Macedonia_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hora_(dance)"},{"title":"Montenegrin Oro","blocks":[{"text":"Crnogorsko oro, or simply oro is a Montenegrin national folk dance originating in the Dinaric region of the Western Balkans. The name 'oro' derives from the dialectal form of the word 'orao', meaning 'eagle', referring to how the dance is performed to resemble the movements of an eagle."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Montenegrin_Oro"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Stamp_of_Moldova_md423.jpg/250px-Stamp_of_Moldova_md423.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/34/Stamp_of_Moldova_md423.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Stamp_of_Moldova_md423.jpg/250px-Stamp_of_Moldova_md423.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStamp_of_Moldova_md423.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Hora_din_Dealul_Spirei%2C_1857.jpg/500px-Hora_din_D